From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] OAM manager: the entries not used this frame hidden
 (SDK_PORT_3DS)

The OAM manager parks the entries it didn't use this frame at y 192,
under the DS's screen, keeping their size, tiles and x. The 3DS port's
lower menu shows a screen laid out 248 lines tall in its panel (the bag),
lines 192-247 too, so the parked entries showed there: the list's red
cursor and the bag, scrambled at the bottom whenever the bag hid them for
a moment (switching pockets). They're hidden outright too (attr0's
disable bit): on the DS they don't show either way. (The unused affine
parameters are reset to 192 as before.)

---
diff --git a/libraries/g2d/src/g2d_OAM.c b/libraries/g2d/src/g2d_OAM.c
index 1ca31e7..36d04a5 100644
--- a/libraries/g2d/src/g2d_OAM.c
+++ b/libraries/g2d/src/g2d_OAM.c
@@ -9,7 +9,18 @@
 NNS_G2D_DEFINE_NNSI_OBJSIZEWTBL;
 NNS_G2D_DEFINE_NNSI_OBJSIZEHTBL;
 
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+// The OAM entries not used this frame are parked at y 192, under the DS's
+// screen; on the 3DS port's taller lower screen (a screen laid out 248
+// lines tall: the lower menu's panel) lines 192-247 are shown, so the
+// parked entries (their size and tiles as before) showed there. They're
+// hidden outright (attr0's disable bit): on the DS they don't show either way.
+#define OAM_SETTING_INVISIBLE   (192 | 0x0200)
+#define OAM_AFFINE_RESET        192 // (the unused affine parameters: as before)
+#else
 #define OAM_SETTING_INVISIBLE   192
+#define OAM_AFFINE_RESET        OAM_SETTING_INVISIBLE
+#endif
 
 #define NUM_HW_OAM_ATTR         128
 #define NUM_HW_OAM_AFFINE       32
@@ -421,10 +432,10 @@ static NNS_G2D_INLINE void ResetAffine_ (NNSG2dOamType type, u16 fromIdx, u16 to
     u16 i;
 
     for (i = 0; i < numArea; i++) {
-        pFrom->PA = OAM_SETTING_INVISIBLE;
-        pFrom->PB = OAM_SETTING_INVISIBLE;
-        pFrom->PC = OAM_SETTING_INVISIBLE;
-        pFrom->PD = OAM_SETTING_INVISIBLE;
+        pFrom->PA = OAM_AFFINE_RESET;
+        pFrom->PB = OAM_AFFINE_RESET;
+        pFrom->PC = OAM_AFFINE_RESET;
+        pFrom->PD = OAM_AFFINE_RESET;
         pFrom++;
     }
 }
